{
  "_comment": "Negative effect roll definitions - same dual-slot shape as positive-effects.data.json: slot 1 picks ONE effect (weighted by each effect's own `chance` among enabled ones - defaults to 1/equal weight if omitted, but always set it explicitly here so the Settings UI's 'Chance %' field, which multiplies chance by 100 assuming it's already a fraction of 1 like positive-effects.data.json's own values, doesn't show a meaningless '100%' for everything). Currently an even 1/6 (0.1667) each. Slot 2 rolls that effect's own value, UNLESS `hasValueRoll` is false (Drop Weapon / Empty Pockets), in which case there's no second roll at all - the effect is single-shot. `min`/`max` roll a plain random value in that range; `bonuses` is the same at-most-one-applies array positive-effects.cjs uses (add/multiply), rolled on TOP of that base value. Time Factor is shaped like Immortality: `min`/`max` roll the DURATION in seconds - the actual speed multiplier isn't rolled/shown as slot 2 at all, `ranges` just picks one of the two disjoint speed bands (slower or faster, never in between) behind the scenes each time it fires. Alcohol rolls a plain `min`/`max` amount, then its own bonus on top. Empty Pockets' `moneyItems` (id + ruble value, real GAMMA money-prop sections) mirrors the MONEY_PROP_ITEMS table in the Lua bridge, which greedily breaks the lost amount into these denominations and drops them on the ground near the actor - the JS side never sends the breakdown, EMPTY_POCKETS is still a bare command, the Lua handler works it out from actor:money() itself. Junk Item is a second effect whose slot 2 IS the item roll: `items` is a flat list of `{id, label, icon, count?}` (count defaults to 1) - picks one at random and gives that many via GIVE_JUNK. Real GAMMA/Anomaly item ids only where relevant - unknown sections are just skipped in-game rather than crashing anything.",
